BT /F2 17 Tf 54 730.0 Td (Access Control Policy) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 697.0 Td (1. Purpose and Scope) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 674.0 Td (This Access Control Policy establishes the requirements Hewlett Packard Enterprise \(HPE\) applies to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 660.0 Td (govern logical access to its information systems, applications, cloud services, and data. It applies) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 646.0 Td (to all HPE employees, contractors, service partners, and third parties who are granted access to HPE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 632.0 Td (resources. The policy covers the full identity lifecycle and the technical and administrative) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 618.0 Td (controls that enforce appropriate, authorized, and auditable access across the enterprise.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 592.0 Td (2. Guiding Principles) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 569.0 Td (HPE governs access according to the principles of least privilege, minimum necessary, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 555.0 Td (need-to-know. Individuals are granted only the access required to perform their assigned duties, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 541.0 Td (no more. Access is denied by default and explicitly granted through approved processes. HPE adopts a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 527.0 Td (zero trust posture in which no user, device, or network location is inherently trusted; every access) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 513.0 Td (request is authenticated, authorized, and continuously evaluated before and during a session.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 487.0 Td (3. Identity Lifecycle Management) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.5 Tf 54 460.0 Td (3.1 Provisioning and Onboarding) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 438.5 Td (Identities are managed centrally through Microsoft Entra ID \(integrated with on-premises Active) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 424.5 Td (Directory\) and federated to applications via Okta as the enterprise single sign-on and identity) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 410.5 Td (provider. During onboarding, Human Resources initiates the joiner event, which triggers automated) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 396.5 Td (provisioning of a user account and baseline entitlements based on the individual's role, department,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 382.5 Td (and location. All access beyond the baseline requires a formal request submitted through the access) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 368.5 Td (management workflow, with approval and authorization from the appropriate resource owner and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 354.5 Td (requester's manager before entitlements are granted.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.5 Tf 54 330.5 Td (3.2 Changes and Movers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 309.0 Td (When a worker changes roles, entitlements are recalculated and prior access that is no longer needed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 295.0 Td (is removed to prevent privilege accumulation. Managers and resource owners are responsible for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 281.0 Td (validating that mover access aligns with the new role.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.5 Tf 54 257.0 Td (3.3 Deprovisioning, Offboarding, and Termination) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 235.5 Td (Upon termination, resignation, or contract completion, HR triggers the leaver event, and accounts) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 221.5 Td (are automatically disabled in Entra ID and Okta, revoking single sign-on and downstream application) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 207.5 Td (access. Deprovisioning during offboarding includes prompt account disablement, revocation of tokens) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 193.5 Td (and sessions, and suspension of federated access. Accounts that are inactive beyond 45 days are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 179.5 Td (automatically flagged for locking and review. Dormant, orphaned, and unused accounts are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 165.5 Td (periodically identified and disabled.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 139.5 Td (4. Role-Based Access Control) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 116.5 Td (HPE uses role-based access control \(RBAC\) to standardize entitlements. Access is assigned to Entra) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 102.5 Td (ID and Active Directory security groups and Okta application roles rather than to individuals, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 88.5 Td (privileges are bundled into roles that map to job functions. Segregation of duties \(SoD\) controls) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 74.5 Td (are enforced to ensure that no single individual can execute conflicting or high-risk) Tj ET
endstream
