BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738.0 Td (transactions-such as requesting and approving the same access, or developing and deploying to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 724.0 Td (production-without independent oversight. Toxic-combination rules are evaluated at request time and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 710.0 Td (during recertification.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 684.0 Td (5. Privileged Access Management) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 661.0 Td (Privileged access-including admin, root, and other elevated entitlements-is tightly restricted,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 647.0 Td (granted only under least privilege, and managed through a Privileged Access Management \(PAM\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 633.0 Td (solution. Privileged credentials are vaulted, rotated, and issued just-in-time with time-bound) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 619.0 Td (elevation and session recording. Administrators use dedicated privileged accounts separate from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 605.0 Td (their standard identities, and multi-factor authentication is mandatory for all elevated actions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 591.0 Td (Service accounts are inventoried, assigned to an accountable owner, restricted to their intended) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 577.0 Td (purpose, and reviewed regularly; interactive logon and unnecessary privileges are prohibited, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 563.0 Td (secrets are stored in an approved vault.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 537.0 Td (6. Remote and Network Access) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 514.0 Td (Remote access to HPE systems is permitted only through approved, encrypted channels. VPN) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 500.0 Td (connectivity and zero trust network access enforce device posture checks, identity verification, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 486.0 Td (conditional access before granting network access. Conditional access policies in Entra ID evaluate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 472.0 Td (risk signals-user, device, location, and behavior-and may require step-up authentication or block) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 458.0 Td (access. All remote sessions are subject to logging and monitoring.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 432.0 Td (7. Access Reviews and Recertification) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 409.0 Td (HPE conducts periodic reviews of access to confirm that entitlements remain appropriate. Access) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 395.0 Td (reviews and recertification campaigns require managers and resource owners to perform attestation of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 381.0 Td (each user's entitlements at least quarterly for privileged and high-risk access and at least) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 367.0 Td (annually for standard access. Entitlements that are not affirmatively recertified are revoked.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 353.0 Td (Review results are documented and retained as audit evidence.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 327.0 Td (8. Monitoring, Logging, and Auditing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 304.0 Td (Authentication and authorization events across Entra ID, Active Directory, Okta, and the PAM) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 290.0 Td (platform are captured through centralized logging and forwarded to HPE's SIEM for monitoring,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 276.0 Td (correlation, and retention. Audit trails support investigations and compliance reporting. Automated) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 262.0 Td (alerting and anomaly detection identify suspicious behavior-such as impossible-travel logins,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 248.0 Td (brute-force attempts, privilege escalation, and anomalous service-account activity-and trigger) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 234.0 Td (response actions, including account locking or suspension pending investigation.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 208.0 Td (9. Enforcement and Review) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 185.0 Td (Violations of this policy may result in revocation of access and disciplinary action up to and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 171.0 Td (including termination. This policy is reviewed at least annually and updated to reflect changes in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 157.0 Td (technology, regulation, and business requirements.) Tj ET
endstream
